  "body": "I'm working with django as an API like and reactjs for client side.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to make a POST request and as I've to send the csrf token I'm facing this issue:\r\n\r\n```\r\nreturn fetch(endpoint, {\r\n\tmethod: req,\r\n\theaders: {\r\n                'Content-Type': 'application/json',\r\n                'X-CSRF-Token': csrfToken,\r\n        },\r\n\tbody: JSON.stringify(data),\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut I'm having this error from chrome:\r\n\r\n> Fetch API [...] Request header field x-csrf-token is not allowed by Access-Control-Allow-Headers in preflight response.\r\n\r\nI don't find something working from the web.. Any ideas?",
